# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and adjust as needed.
# yahoo-finance2 needs no API key — these are optional tuning knobs.

# REQUIRED for real 5/10-Year and "All Available" chart history.
#
# SEC EDGAR (lib/finance/providers/sec-edgar.ts) is the only source deep
# enough to back a genuine 10-year+ range selection — Yahoo Finance's free
# fundamentalsTimeSeries API has a hard, undocumented backend cap of ~4
# annual periods / ~5 quarters *no matter what date range is requested*, so
# without SEC EDGAR working, every range selector above ~4 years silently
# renders the same ~4 years of data.
#
# SEC EDGAR requires every request to declare a real contact in its
# User-Agent header — confirmed directly against SEC's official Developer
# FAQ (sec.gov/about/webmaster-frequently-asked-questions#developers,
# "Developers" section): "Please declare your user agent in request
# headers", sample shape "Sample Company Name AdminContact@<sample company
# domain>.com". There's no SEC-sanctioned way around this — it's not a
# best-practice suggestion, it's how EDGAR decides whether to serve you or
# return a 403 "Undeclared Automated Tool" error.
#
# Leaving this unset does NOT break the app: lib/finance/providers/sec-edgar.ts
# ships a built-in default shaped exactly like SEC's own sample, every SEC
# fetch has a request timeout, and any SEC failure (403, timeout, or
# anything else) is treated as "SEC EDGAR unavailable" and silently falls
# back to Yahoo's data — which works, just capped at ~4 years no matter the
# range selected. Set this to a real app name + email you control to
# actually get 10+ years of history and avoid sharing the built-in
# default's rate-limit exposure with every other unmodified deployment:
#   SEC_EDGAR_CONTACT="Your App Name you@yourdomain.com"
SEC_EDGAR_CONTACT=

# How long quotes/search results are cached in-process before refetching (ms).
MARKET_DATA_CACHE_TTL_MS=20000

# Optional secondary data source (lib/finance/providers/fmp.ts). Backfills
# cash-flow fields (stock-based comp, capex) when Yahoo's free tier omits
# them for a given ticker. Get a free key at financialmodelingprep.com —
# leave unset and FinLens runs Yahoo-only with no loss of functionality.
FMP_API_KEY=

# --- Multi-User Authentication & Data Isolation (lib/db/client.ts) -------
#
# This app's user/session/portfolio database is Postgres, hosted on Neon.
# There is deliberately no "zero-config local file" fallback (unlike an
# earlier version of this app, which used Turso/SQLite): Vercel's
# serverless functions have a read-only, ephemeral filesystem, so a file on
# disk cannot correctly back multi-user data once deployed there — that's
# true no matter how the file is created, so rather than let it silently
# "work" on one machine and break in production, the app fails loudly with
# a clear error (see dbErrorJson in lib/http/noStore.ts) if this isn't set.
#
# Setup — no CLI, no separate account signup, nothing to copy/paste:
#   1. Open your project in the Vercel dashboard -> Storage tab
#   2. Click "Create Database" / "Add Integration" -> choose Neon
#   3. Follow the prompts (this creates a Neon account + Postgres database
#      for you automatically) and confirm
# That's it — Vercel automatically injects DATABASE_URL (and the legacy
# POSTGRES_URL alias) into this project's Production, Preview, AND
# Development environments. Nothing to paste into Environment Variables
# by hand.
#
# For local development, pull that same value down instead of retyping it:
#   npm i -g vercel   (one-time)
#   vercel link       (one-time, connects this folder to the Vercel project)
#   vercel env pull .env.development.local
# Or, if you'd rather skip the CLI entirely, open the Vercel dashboard's
# Environment Variables page and copy DATABASE_URL's value into your own
# .env.local by hand.
DATABASE_URL=
